Aerie-Purpose: Make WebGL and WebGPU in workers follow the per-site and global switches instead of always masking, now that Helium gives every worker its page's or site's noise tokens.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: third_party/blink/renderer/core/execution_context/gpu_info_masking.h, content/browser/worker_host/mock_shared_worker.*
Aerie-Kind: hook

Follows hardening/0010 (issue #113, part of #87). Helium 0.22 (core/noise/core.patch) derives the tokens of a
dedicated worker (from its creator), a shared worker and a service worker (from the top-level site of their
storage key, with the same ContentBrowserClient::HeliumNoiseEnabled decision as a navigation) and sends them in
the worker start parameters. Earlier Aerie patches (hardening/0013 and the transport half of this one) did the
same and are gone. What stays is the GPU masking helper: ShouldMaskGpuInfoForContext (hardening/0010) no longer
treats a worker as always masked. A window or a worker follows its kWebGL token, so protection turned off for
the browser or the site reaches the worker, and only a null context stays fail closed.

The test mock of the shared worker factory takes the new last argument that Helium's mojom method has.

--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/execution_context/gpu_info_masking.h
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/execution_context/gpu_info_masking.h
@@ -14,17 +14,17 @@
 namespace blink {
 
 // Whether WebGL and WebGPU report masked graphics card details to this context
-// (Aerie, issue #112). A null context counts as a worker. A worker has no noise
-// tokens yet, so it is always protected while the features are on (fail
-// closed, until issue #113).
+// (Aerie, issue #112). A window and a worker both follow their kWebGL token: a
+// worker has the tokens of its page or site (issue #113), so protection turned
+// off for the site or the browser reaches it. A null context has no token to
+// read, so it is protected while the features are on (fail closed).
 inline bool ShouldMaskGpuInfoForContext(const ExecutionContext* context) {
-  const bool is_worker = !context || context->IsWorkerOrWorkletGlobalScope();
   const bool has_token =
       context &&
       context->GetHeliumNoiseTokens().contains(HeliumNoiseFeature::kWebGL);
   return aerie_gpu_info::ShouldMaskGpuInfo(
-      is_worker ? aerie_gpu_info::ContextKind::kWorker
-                : aerie_gpu_info::ContextKind::kWindow,
+      context ? aerie_gpu_info::ContextKind::kExecutionContext
+              : aerie_gpu_info::ContextKind::kNoContext,
       {.master_enabled = base::FeatureList::IsEnabled(features::kHeliumNoise),
        .surface_enabled =
            base::FeatureList::IsEnabled(features::kHeliumNoiseWebGL),
